      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFix LoRA server startup on older Triton versions. With `triton-ascend 3.2.2` (Triton module version `3.2.0`), decode graph capture fails while compiling the ragged cSGMV expand kernel:\n\n```text\ntiles = (SLICE_OFFSETS[s + 1] - SLICE_OFFSETS[s] + BLOCK_N - 1) // BLOCK_N\nTypeError(\"'constexpr' object is not subscriptable\")\n```\n\nThis blocks both LoRA update tests before their assertions in [the failing NPU CI job](https://github.com/Ascend/sglang/actions/runs/41192732188/job/124512664305). The older `tl.constexpr` wrapper does not implement tuple subscription, and its compiler evaluates the subscript directly.\n\n## Modifications\n\nRead each slice boundary from the wrapped tuple's `.value`, then wrap the scalar with `tl.constexpr` for compile-time arithmetic. Reuse the two boundaries for tile sizing and slice selection. The ragged grid, fallback path, cache key, and launch configuration remain unchanged; no device copies or kernel launches are added.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nValidated on Ascend A3 / CANN 9.1.0, Torch `2.10.0+cpu`, torch_npu `2.10.0.post6`, and triton-ascend `3.2.2`, using runtime commit `93f4f1a87dbf356833e5d2ec777ee4b006b631fd`. The original expand kernel is byte-for-byte identical to the kernel at this PR's upstream base, `c8704818d4f04fa9249a4144f14882670b4d37ae`.\n\n| Check | Result |\n| --- | --- |\n| Original / patched minimal reproducer | Original reproduces the compilation error (exit 1); patched passes (exit 0). |\n| Torch reference comparison | 10 configurations pass for both ragged and rectangular fallback paths, including mixed ranks, zero rank, strided outputs, and no base output. FP16 maximum absolute error: `0.000244140625` (`atol=rtol=0.003`). |\n| BF16 Llama GQA dimensions | Q/K/V widths `4096/1024/1024`, ranks `256/32`: maximum absolute error `0.015625` (`atol=rtol=0.03`). |\n| NPU graph capture/replay | BF16, rank 16, batch sizes 1/2/4: exactly matches eager output. |\n| Serving smoke test | Llama 3.2 1B with synthetic rank-4/rank-8 adapters, five prompts each: dynamic/static loading yields identical token IDs in 10/10 comparisons. Load/list/generate/unload and adapter-effect checks pass; decode uses NPU graphs. |\n\nThe complete fresh upstream checkout was not run on NPU. The original CI's Llama 3.1 8B and four real adapters were unavailable, so the original full test matrix was not rerun. CUDA GPU execution was not tested.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nA same-stack operator comparison used the working rectangular fallback as a reference, with rank 16, 16 tokens, 10 warmups, and 30 measurements of 20 calls per path. Median rectangular / patched-ragged times in microseconds were: unequal QKV `193.00 / 180.83`, equal QKV `207.59 / 208.78`, two-slice MLP `202.24 / 200.21`, and single slice `152.76 / 153.07`.\n\nEvent timings include host launch gaps, and paths were measured in a fixed order. This is not a before/after comparison with the original ragged path, which cannot compile on this stack. No serving throughput benchmark or profiling was run, and no end-to-end performance improvement is claimed.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Targeted lint and formatting pass with the repository-pinned Ruff 0.15.1 and isort 7.0.0; `git diff --check` passes.\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the contribution guide. No new repository test files are included; operator and serving validation is summarized above.\n- [x] Provide accuracy and operator timing results, including their coverage limits.\n- [x] Follow the existing kernel code style. No public API or configuration changes require documentation updates.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41579177993](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41579177993)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41579178110](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41579178110)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41579178127](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41579178127)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
